 "note": "an orthographic projector over a wall and a box",
 "gaps": [
  "three.js body: the projection is GLSL added by onBeforeCompile to every mesh material the body makes (one shared set of uniforms, up to four projectors, nearest texel through textureLod); a shape drawn by a ShaderMaterial is not tinted",
  "a shape drawn by a ShaderMaterial (a ComposedShader, volume or Texturing3D mesh) is not tinted; X_ITE 16.6.0 tints those too; points and lines are not tinted either",
  "PhysicalMaterial (MeshPhysicalMaterial) gets the same tint of its diffuse colour before the lights; not compared by picture here (the Babylon fixture could not show it)",
  "upVector default: X3DUOM 4.0 says 0 1 0 (used here); X_ITE 16.6.0 reads 0 0 1 for a scene whose version is 4.0 or lower, so a tilted projector with no upVector written is rolled differently there",
  "at most four projectors at a time (X_ITE's maxTextures), the first four that are on; the picture is read nearest-texel, mip levels and TextureProperties filters are not applied (X_ITE's default look is nearest as well)",
  "shadows, shadowColor, shadowIntensity and shadowMapSize are stored and do nothing (X_ITE 16.6.0 does not shadow a projector either)"
 ],
